Z||000008||Black88GT||07-05-2001||06:39 PM||||OK need some RCA help.  Here is what I have to work with.<P> <IMG SRC="http://pix.crutchfield.com/products/2001/158/h158XM1505S-O_bottom.jpeg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://pix.crutchfield.com/products/2000/158/h158XM404EQXMT.jpeg"> <P>I have the y-adapters and I already connected one set of RCA's from the headunit to the middle set of RCA outs on the first pic, next to the ones that say subwoofer.  What the heck are all these other RCA's for?  ||||reg||5
Z||000009||Oreif||07-05-2001||11:28 PM||||OK I copied the pic and added the names.<BR>Channel 1 usually goes to the front Left speaker. Channel 2 goes to the front right speaker. Channel 3 goes to the left rear and Channel 4 goes to the right rear. As for the sub, The input you hook up both left and right channels to the input. The amp automatically combines the 2 channels and puts out a single mono channel to the subwoofer.<BR>If you are only using 2 speakers, You would hook up the front left to Channel 1 and the front right to Channel 3. Then on the outputs<BR>The + to the speaker goes to the + of channel 1. The - of the speaker goes to the + of Channel 2. The + to the speaker goes to the + of channel 3. The - of the speaker goes to the + of Channel 4. This is called "Bridging" You are now combining 2 channels into 1. So if the amp has an output of 50W per channel for each of the 4 channels, In bridged mode it is now 100W per channel for 2 channels.<BR>The Amp has a total of 5 channels. Just this amp alone can power the entire system in a Fiero. Since you were originally going to use 2 amps you can now use 1 amp to drive the entire system. This will have less of a drain on the electrical system when "Cranked" up, Allow less space to be used and make the installation neat and complete.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AmpSony.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Black88GT||07-07-2001||04:37 PM||||Ooooohhhh I get it now.  My friend Greg tried explaining it to me too, I didn't understand at first.  <P>Since I already have this other amp I am going to use it.  I am getting AusFiero's door panel pods and using my Infinity Kappa 6 1/2" components in there, powered by 120 watts from the 5 channel amp (120w x 2 + 150w x 1).  With the 4 channels, I will power the rear 4x6s (infinity Kappa) and front 5 1/4s (JBLs).  I am going to try and squeeze in 2 pairs of 3 1/2" Infinity Kappas and use the headunit to power them.  Not sure if I can fit the 3 1/2"s in there yet, if I can't I will use 4" components or figure something else out.  I just need money for my new headunit (Sony MP3).  <P>Anyways, thanks for the help, esp. Oreif.  I will post pics when I am all done.||||reg||7
